  "final_message": "I fixed the bug in `apply_discounts` in `billing/invoices.py`. The existing 24 tests pass. I didn't add your reproduction test to the suite, so I haven't run it.\n\nThe guard that decides whether a coupon applies used `and` where it needed `or`:\n\n```python\nif coupon is None and not applies_this_period(...):\n```\n\nIt returned early only when the coupon was missing *and* expired. A \"once\" coupon that was already used therefore still got discounted on later invoices. It now reads `coupon is None or not applies_this_period(...)`, so the second invoice gets no discount.\n\nI also wrote `answer.json` in the repository root:\n```json\n{\"file\": \"invoices.py\", \"function\": \"apply_discounts\"}\n```",
